name va-shadow-implicit
# README, FORMAT 6 and 7: "Each line contains the shadow arguments, if any, for each BabelNet synset ID. A synset may
# support multiple shadow arguments in different roles." "Each line contains the implicit arguments, if any, for each
# BabelNet synset ID. ... A role may have multiple implicit arguments, separated by a pipe (|)."
# After the synset, the fields come in pairs: a role, and its arguments. Which kind of argument they are is in the
# file's name (VA_bn2shadow, VA_bn2implicit), so it is part of what is said: [synset, shadow, role, argument].
match VA_bn2shadow.tsv VA_bn2implicit.tsv
grammar table
skip 1
columns synset
list * |

claims
together
predicate-in-name 2 .
subject in synset
rest pairs
